From: Ben Joldersma <bennidhamma@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 02:27:04 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] [COSMIC] Follow COSMIC's glass opacity setting

COSMIC lets users choose how see-through its frosted windows are
(Settings > Desktop > Appearance > Glass opacity). It stores a
"frosted" strength in its theme config, which the theme's "alpha_map"
maps to the alpha of window backgrounds.

CosmicGlassSettings reads and watches these config entries (and the
light/dark mode) on a blocking sequence when the desktop is COSMIC.
GlassFrameService::AdjustTintOpacityForDesktop() scales how much of the
blurred backdrop the glass frame's tint lets through by the same factor
COSMIC's own windows use relative to its default strength, so the
browser follows the slider live.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
